.TH smi-forward "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-forward \- Switch the port forwarding of 80 and 443 between nginx and HAProxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-forward
.BR nginx | haproxy
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-forward
points the privileged ports of the
.B public
firewalld zone at one of the two web fronts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nginx      80 -> 8080    443 -> 8081
haproxy    80 -> 8090    443 -> 8091
.fi
.RE
.PP
The rules of the other one are removed first, so the two never forward the same port at once, and
each switch is made twice: in the running configuration and, with
.BR --permanent ,
in the stored one, so it survives a reload and a reboot without a
.B firewall-cmd --reload
of its own.
.PP
Each port is forwarded twice as well: with a
.B forward-port
rule, which firewalld applies to IPv4, and with the matching
.B rich-rule
of
.BR "family=ipv6" ,
so a request over IPv6 lands on the same web front.
.PP
Removing a rule that is not there is not an error, so the command can be run when the other front
was never forwarded, or twice in a row.
Adding has to succeed; the command stops at the first failure.
The forwarded ports and the rich rules of the zone are printed at the end.
.PP
It has to be run as root, and firewalld has to be installed and running.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B nginx
Forward to 8080 and 8081, the nginx ports.
.TP
.B haproxy
Forward to 8090 and 8091, the HAProxy ports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zone forwards to the chosen web front.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong or missing argument, not root, no
.BR firewall-cmd ,
or firewalld is not running.
.TP
.I other
Exit status of
.BR firewall-cmd (1)
for a failed addition.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Serve the sites straight from nginx:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-forward nginx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Put HAProxy in front, for example to give draft previews their cookie check:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-forward haproxy
.fi
.RE
.PP
What is forwarded now:
.RS
.nf
sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --list-forward-ports
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.PP
The zone and the four ports are fixed in the command, matching the nginx and HAProxy
configuration of the web front: nginx listens on 8080 and 8081, HAProxy on 8090 and 8091, and
neither needs a privileged port of its own.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
